---
description: Require TypeScript instead of plain JavaScript
alwaysApply: true
---

# TypeScript Only

- Use TypeScript for all new code in this app.
- Do not create new `.js` or `.jsx` source files.
- Prefer `.ts` and `.tsx` for new modules, components, hooks, utilities, and tests.
- When editing an existing JavaScript source file, prefer converting it to TypeScript instead of extending the JavaScript version when the scope is reasonable.
- Avoid plain JavaScript patterns such as untyped props, `any`-like loose data flow, and implicit object shapes when a typed alternative is available.
